                        "target_lang_word": "Bandit",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Bandit",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5e8e2a43-72a4-3067-a1b3-deac9cef46f9",
                                        "entry_id": "fcaa617f-f758-3fc4-9caf-ea1604870073",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Verbrecher, Straßenräuber, der meist einer kriminellen Gruppe angehört"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26f2ff04-9285-4bd6-8498-9a286c959a33",
                                                "sense_id": "5e8e2a43-72a4-3067-a1b3-deac9cef46f9",
                                                "text": "„O schreiben Sie mir, selbst wenn Sie krank sein sollten; seitdem ich keinen Brief von Ihnen erhalten habe, seh ich nichts als Räuber und Banditen, die Sie überfallen und ermorden […] – o schreiben Sie mir ja sogleich, mir treten oft kalte Tränen des Entsetzens in die Augen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95390bd7-284f-482b-bded-1298b0fdbee4",
                                                "sense_id": "5e8e2a43-72a4-3067-a1b3-deac9cef46f9",
                                                "text": "„Die Banditen durchsuchen seinen Tornister und finden nichts als Bücher, trockenes Brot, harten Käse, zwei Hemden und ein Notizbuch.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c9c53c03-a89f-4d7e-b778-35299b8d3c7f",
                                                "sense_id": "5e8e2a43-72a4-3067-a1b3-deac9cef46f9",
                                                "text": "„In dem herrschenden Vakuum regierten Banditen die Straßen.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b4ffbbf2-bf91-4fbf-ab1a-d8d0e984d4f8",
                                                "sense_id": "5e8e2a43-72a4-3067-a1b3-deac9cef46f9",
                                                "text": "„So ein erfolgreicher Bandit schwimmt doch nur so im Geld.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "18e915eb-eb27-417e-82ef-839553e4b681",
                        "source_entry_id": "80cfd455-4c4c-3b9b-8fbc-21c6fce456d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "9869d53c-ba67-3d9b-b930-168e0b6cc401",
                        "source_sense_description": "een schurk of misdadiger",
                        "target_lang_word": "bandit",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bandit",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1c65fb72-a97f-3ffe-9112-4ef1fafb9a84",
                                        "entry_id": "4bb5a215-ab1a-351a-a168-8a9184fa2809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who robs others in a lawless area, especially as part of a group."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c4b13db-c6ac-4808-80b3-8d9693220f00",
                                                "sense_id": "1c65fb72-a97f-3ffe-9112-4ef1fafb9a84",
                                                "text": "Do you recollect a story my nurse told us of a Sicilian bandit, the terror of the country?—how he saved a young child from a cottage on fire, brought it up delicately, and far removed from his own pursuits; while, at his execution, his chief regret was the future provision for that boy?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27df473d-a5e7-3f2a-89b4-f46bc8eb5328",
                                        "entry_id": "4bb5a215-ab1a-351a-a168-8a9184fa2809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An outlaw."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0f90e51e-e32e-336b-9ac6-139a93fb11b3",
                                        "entry_id": "4bb5a215-ab1a-351a-a168-8a9184fa2809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "One who cheats others."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b799bfbe-37db-36fb-a357-b49e69373e64",
                                        "entry_id": "4bb5a215-ab1a-351a-a168-8a9184fa2809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An aircraft identified as an enemy, but distinct from \\\"hostile\\\" or \\\"threat\\\" in that it is not immediately to be engaged."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10b33389-086b-348d-bd1e-1f35d1a7505c",
                                        "entry_id": "4bb5a215-ab1a-351a-a168-8a9184fa2809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A runner who covertly joins a race without having registered as a participant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "656baf2c-7578-3e3e-8a35-190bf1d58dc4",
                                        "entry_id": "4bb5a215-ab1a-351a-a168-8a9184fa2809",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Synonym of arse bandit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "UK",
                                            "dated",
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "bandit",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "022cf3a2-47a6-3fac-8f09-a32abd734a8f",
                                        "entry_id": "b6a72079-d075-3cbc-a41b-c2cafcffd6cc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To rob, or steal from, in the manner of a bandit."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "ambitransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1969d228-0c75-4602-a3b8-d5c27fef7136",
                                                "sense_id": "022cf3a2-47a6-3fac-8f09-a32abd734a8f",
                                                "text": "First, she read the bandit news in the paper, and was rather disappointed to learn that her man had evidently taken a night off from banditing. An imitator of the bandit had made an unsuccessful attempt to hold up a drug-store, and had backed out and run when the nervy proprietor reached for a gun; but that was all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42384098-ebc5-403d-8a8b-93969c8b4b87",
                                                "sense_id": "022cf3a2-47a6-3fac-8f09-a32abd734a8f",
                                                "text": "As the sanctuary was bandited at least once, it may be that the silver wine cups I have are from the treasure."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "448da728-e0e5-4d3e-8fcc-806d0a8691f1",
                        "source_entry_id": "80cfd455-4c4c-3b9b-8fbc-21c6fce456d1",
                        "source_sense_id": "9869d53c-ba67-3d9b-b930-168e0b6cc401",
                        "source_sense_description": "een schurk of misdadiger",
                        "target_lang_word": "bandit",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bandit",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "284d7c24-c0a4-350c-8506-0579fcaa27ea",
                                        "entry_id": "6447e91d-ee0b-39ca-aec7-a76655396505",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Malfaiteur vagabond et armé."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dcfc9d28-caaf-4b70-beaa-060a60cb6192",
                                                "sense_id": "284d7c24-c0a4-350c-8506-0579fcaa27ea",
                                                "text": "L’enragé qu’il était, né roi d’une province\nQu’il pouvait gouverner en bon et sage prince,\nS’en alla follement, et pensant être dieu,\nCourir comme un bandit qui n’a ni feu ni lieu ;\nEt, traînant avec soi les horreurs de la guerre,\nDe sa vaste folie emplir toute la terre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b32f561-2264-4357-9401-f3c22c493fbc",
                                                "sense_id": "284d7c24-c0a4-350c-8506-0579fcaa27ea",
                                                "text": "Vos bandits sont des crapules, de la basse fripouille. Les nôtres sont d’honnêtes gens."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "052acade-2fda-476d-8a08-8f1a30ab3e69",
                                                "sense_id": "284d7c24-c0a4-350c-8506-0579fcaa27ea",
                                                "text": "De héros épique, Mémed devient bandit d’honneur : c’est sa manière d’entrer dans la légende, en conciliant son impossible retour avec son aura."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d46fe42-416b-4a2d-92d5-69a3636984c0",
                                                "sense_id": "284d7c24-c0a4-350c-8506-0579fcaa27ea",
                                                "text": "En plus, son papa, qui a parfois des idées saugrenues, lui raconte l’histoire de la cour des Miracles, le repaire au Moyen Âge de tous les voleurs, tire-laine et autres bandits qui infestaient la ville de Paris."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "08f72695-f871-4a95-849b-55d3b71dff8e",
                                                "sense_id": "284d7c24-c0a4-350c-8506-0579fcaa27ea",
                                                "text": "Dès la fin des années 1880, en effet, des « bandits » se prévalent de l’anarchisme pour opérer non des vols ou des cambriolages, mais des « reprises individuelles »."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d0131d37-bba4-3d0e-b081-51dfabb096bf",
                                        "entry_id": "6447e91d-ee0b-39ca-aec7-a76655396505",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Personne sans aveu."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ca82ecc8-7041-4b46-9d6e-63c28d2d4ef9",
                                                "sense_id": "d0131d37-bba4-3d0e-b081-51dfabb096bf",
                                                "text": "Et il y avait encore, dans ses yeux, l’horrible étonnement d’une nature douce et inoffensive s’apercevant, à la dernière heure, des infamies de ce monde, frissonnant à la pensée des longues années passées côte à côte avec un bandit."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
